{"name":"Master Sword Blue","hex":"#00ffee","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"master","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Someone who has control over something or someone.","The owner of an animal or slave."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Masterful.","Main, principal or predominant."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/master"},{"term":"sword","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A long bladed weapon with a grip and typically a pommel and crossguard (together forming a hilt), which is designed to cut, stab, slash and/or hack.","A suit in certain playing card decks, particularly those used in Spain and Italy, or those used for divination.\nA card of this suit."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To stab or cut with a sword"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sword"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Master Sword","blocks":[{"text":"The Master Sword  is a fictional divine magic sword in Nintendo's The Legend of Zelda series. At times, it is referred to in-universe as the \"blade of evil's bane\" or the \"sword that seals the darkness\". It was introduced in the 1991 action-adventure video game The Legend of Zelda: A Link to the Past and has since appeared in most other games in the series."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/f/f9/Master_Sword_Lead.png/330px-Master_Sword_Lead.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Master_Sword","wikidata":"Q2203334"},{"title":"Sword","blocks":[{"text":"A sword is an edged, bladed weapon intended for manual cutting or thrusting. Its blade, longer than that of a knife or dagger, is attached to a hilt and can be straight or curved. A thrusting sword tends to have a straighter blade with a pointed tip. A slashing sword is more likely to be curved and to have a sharpened cutting edge on one or both sides of the blade. Many swords are designed for both thrusting and slashing. The precise definition of a sword varies by historical epoch and geographic region."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sword","wikidata":"Q12791"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9c/Master_Sword.png/330px-Master_Sword.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9c/Master_Sword.png/330px-Master_Sword.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Artwork of the Master Sword for The Legend of Zelda: A Link to the Past","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMaster_Sword.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/New_York_Comic_Con_2013_-_Link_%2810275648465%29.jpg/500px-New_York_Comic_Con_2013_-_Link_%2810275648465%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/New_York_Comic_Con_2013_-_Link_%2810275648465%29.jpg/1280px-New_York_Comic_Con_2013_-_Link_%2810275648465%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/New_York_Comic_Con_2013_-_Link_%2810275648465%29.jpg/500px-New_York_Comic_Con_2013_-_Link_%2810275648465%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A cosplayer dressed as Link holding the Master Sword and the Hylian Shield. These two components have become integral aspects of the character's identity.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANew_York_Comic_Con_2013_-_Link_(10275648465).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Espadon-Morges.jpg/330px-Espadon-Morges.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Espadon-Morges.jpg/330px-Espadon-Morges.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Swiss longsword, 15th or 16th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEspadon-Morges.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg/500px-Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg/1280px-Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Western_Han_Iron_Sword.jpg/500px-Western_Han